From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 21:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: the AP-mode debugfs unregister was never compiled in

Every re-association of an already-seen MAC logged:

    debugfs: '08:5b:d6:d9:c2:13' already exists in 'rc'
    aicwf_sdio mmc1:6721:1: Error while (un)registering debug entry for sta 7

Deterministically, on every cycle, with the sta index climbing for one
unchanging MAC.

The two calls that pair up are guarded by different macros:

    #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS           /* defined - the kernel has debugfs */
            rwnx_dbgfs_register_rc_stat(rwnx_hw, sta);

    #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS_AIC       /* defined NOWHERE */
                rwnx_dbgfs_unregister_rc_stat(rwnx_hw, cur);

CONFIG_DEBUG_FS_AIC does not exist -- not in the Makefile, not in any header,
not in the kernel. Both AP-mode station-delete paths use it, so in AP mode the
register is compiled in and the unregister is compiled out. The MAC-named
directory under rc/ is created on first association and then never removed, and
every later debugfs_create_dir() for that MAC collides. The TDLS path a
thousand lines further down uses plain CONFIG_DEBUG_FS and is unaffected, which
is what makes this look like a typo rather than a decision.

Confirmed on hardware before the fix: after ten forced re-associations the rc/
directory held exactly one entry, timestamped at boot, while the station had
joined and left ten times.

    /sys/kernel/debug/ieee80211/phy0/rwnx/rc/08:5b:d6:d9:c2:13

Use CONFIG_DEBUG_FS in both places.

NOT A RACE, and worth saying plainly because the previous patch in this series
was written on the theory that it was one. The workqueue toggle this goes
through is genuinely fragile and 0008 is worth keeping on its own merits, but
it was never what produced these two lines: an unregister that does not exist
cannot lose a race.

---
diff --git a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
index 580c3c9..5479d51 100644
--- a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -3099,7 +3099,7 @@ static int rwnx_cfg80211_del_station_compat(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 			rwnx_mu_group_sta_del(rwnx_hw, cur);
 #endif /* CONFIG_RWNX_BFMER */
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS_AIC
+#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 			rwnx_dbgfs_unregister_rc_stat(rwnx_hw, cur);
 #endif
 		}
@@ -3213,7 +3213,7 @@ void apm_staloss_work_process(struct work_struct *work)
 		rwnx_mu_group_sta_del(rwnx_hw, cur);
 #endif /* CONFIG_RWNX_BFMER */
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS_AIC
+#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 		rwnx_dbgfs_unregister_rc_stat(rwnx_hw, cur);
 #endif
 	}else {
